# Caddy reverse proxy for the app -- the LAN-facing alternative to Tailscale
# Serve (README, "Reaching it over HTTPS"). Copy to /opt/homebrew/etc/Caddyfile
# and `brew services start caddy`. Caddy runs as your user, not root.
#
# This serves a publicly trusted certificate for assets.rohita.com, issued by
# ACM's managed ACME endpoint and renewed on the Mini by certbot (see
# AGENTS.md's "Deployment topology" for the full issuance/renewal setup and
# scripts/com.assetmgt.certrenew.plist). Because the cert is publicly trusted,
# there's no per-client CA to install, unlike the old `tls internal` setup.
# List the same name in APP_ALLOWED_HOSTS in .env.
#
# Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto on its own; uvicorn trusts
# them only from 127.0.0.1 (see scripts/com.assetmgt.app.plist).

assets.rohita.com {
	tls /Users/YOURUSER/.certbot/config/live/assets.rohita.com/fullchain.pem \
	    /Users/YOURUSER/.certbot/config/live/assets.rohita.com/privkey.pem
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}

# Plain http on the LAN stays closed: nothing listens on :80 for the app, and
# the app itself only listens on loopback.
#
# Have a device that can't reach a public name (fully offline LAN, or a
# client that won't do public DNS)? Fall back to the old local-CA approach:
# a separate site block for a LAN-only name with `tls internal`, trusted
# once per client device with `caddy trust`.
